Licensing (v1.1)
================

Data records are licensed per file according to the license of the arXiv
source paper each record was derived from. Code is licensed under MIT.
Only records whose source license clearly permits redistribution of derived
text are distributed.

1. Data
-------

  File                              Records  Source licenses        Record license
  data/problems_cc_by.jsonl           1,334  CC BY 4.0/3.0, CC0     CC BY 4.0
  data/problems_cc_by_sa.jsonl           43  CC BY-SA 4.0           CC BY-SA 4.0
  data/problems_cc_by_nc_sa.jsonl       165  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0        CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

The *_public.jsonl evaluation cuts (S0/S1/paper-disjoint) contain records
from the three files above; each record keeps its record_license field and is
governed by that license.

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Attribution: cite WirelessMathBench-XL and the source paper identified by each
record's paper_id (arXiv identifier).

Withheld records. 2,485 records derived from papers under the arXiv default
non-exclusive distribution license (2,160), CC BY-NC-ND (323), or with no
recorded license (2) are NOT distributed. data/excluded_records_manifest.csv
lists them by identifier only (problem_id, paper_id, arxiv_id, split, type,
license_class); it contains no problem text.

Identifier-level metadata (contamination_flags_v11.csv,
contamination_metadata.jsonl, s0_membership_by_n.csv,
paper_disjoint_split_seed0.csv, source_paper_licenses.csv, evaluation result
CSVs) contains no source-derived prose and is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
Matched n-gram strings are omitted for withheld records.

Source-paper text is not redistributed and remains governed by the terms chosen
by the respective source-paper authors.

